  "worked_solution": "We write $\\frac{2}{3}$ as $\\frac{4}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}-\\frac{7}{6}=\\frac{4-7}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/d542609ee447bff7bcb3209bb8ea6eccbd770509d2ae4ad794df9eb6606c2b17.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-7}{6}=\\frac{-3}{6}=-\\frac{3}{6}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{6}=-\\frac{3÷3}{6÷3}=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{7}{6}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$",
